  "configuration_id": "config_009",
  "reason": "With no prior experiments, the highest-priority question is establishing a strong multimodal singleprofile baseline to anchor all subsequent comparisons. config_009 (scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l, concat fusion, singleprofile) is chosen because: (1) it pairs a learned RNA embedding (scvi_n200) with a strong pretrained image encoder (ViT-L), representing a well-motivated 'default strong' multimodal setup; (2) concat fusion is the simplest fusion strategy, avoiding confounding from learned weighting; (3) singleprofile keeps the experiment focused on the core question of whether the two modalities, when simply combined, provide a useful signal. This baseline will serve as the reference point for all follow-up experiments testing whether removing a modality (image_only/rna_only), changing the RNA encoder, switching to multiprofile+aggregation, or altering fusion actually improves or degrades performance. Under a limited budget, anchoring the search around a clear, interpretable multimodal reference is more informative than starting with a unimodal baseline (which would leave the multimodal ceiling unknown) or a complex multiprofile configuration (which would conflate multiple design choices)."
}

